{
 "derivation": "Bars: open 100, high 101, low 99, volume 10; close 101 gives est_delta = 10*(202-200)/2 = +10, close 99 gives 10*(198-200)/2 = -10. Bars closing at 1..20 s are bearish (-10), bars closing at 21..40 s are bullish (+10). short_window 5s -> D(5) = sum of the last 5 bars, D(10) = sum of the last 10 bars; acceleration = dir * (2*D(5) - D(10)). Physical alias of the 5s instance is trend_normalized_est_delta_acceleration_5s. T=8s (8 bars): the 10s window needs 10 bars (oldest bar ts 1s > cutoff+1s = -1s) -> unavailable -> null. T=23s, dir=-1: D(5) = bars 19..23 = -10-10+10+10+10 = +10; D(10) = bars 14..23 = 7*(-10)+3*(+10) = -40; 2*10-(-40) = 60; times -1 = -60.0. T=25s, dir=+1: D(5) = bars 21..25 = +50; D(10) = bars 16..25 = -50+50 = 0; 2*50-0 = 100.0. T=26s, no prevailing direction in episode_state -> the adapter emits null. T=30s, dir=+1: D(5) = +50, D(10) = +100; 2*50-100 = 0.0. Bars continue to 40 s so the availability guard is exercised after the last snapshot.",
